# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
**/results/**
# ...except plots under the top-level results/ tree (2026-09-15, user:
# "I especially want the plots to be included so I can download and
# view them") -- pkl/other data files stay ignored everywhere,
# including archive/initial_build/results/ (a separate old archive,
# no plots in it anyway). Two earlier attempts were wrong: "results/*"
# only reached one level deep (staged 1384 nested pkls it should have
# excluded); "results/**", lacking a leading "/", matched ONLY the
# top-level results/ directory (git anchors any pattern with a
# non-trailing "/" to the .gitignore's own directory) and silently
# left archive/initial_build/results/ matching NO rule at all -- not
# re-included, just entirely unignored by omission. The leading "**/"
# here restores "any results/ dir, any depth" for the base ignore; the
# leading "/" on the two lines below then deliberately re-anchors
# THEM to the repo root only, so the re-include is top-level-only.
!/results/**/
!/results/**/*.png
**/scratch_work/*.pkl
**/scratch_work/*.log
*.err
*.out

*.npz

# Sphinx docs build output (source lives in docs/, built by CI --
# .github/workflows/docs.yml -- never committed)
docs/_build/
docs/api/**/*.rst.bak

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Environments
.venv/
venv/

# Claude Code session logs (contains .credentials.json) -- never commit
bh3_claude_output/
